`resolveToken` now falls back to `process.env.API_TOKEN` when no token is passed, and an explicit token still wins. The §explicit-token record is updated to show the override. All 8 tests pass, and the changes are uncommitted in the working tree.

The project has a hook that only accepts an override of a recorded decision when the user named that decision and said to override it. I relied on your brief saying the maintainer explicitly overrode §explicit-token. If that's not exactly what happened, this change should be reverted.

